In a time where the PSP is considered "not really successful" because
Sony sold "only" 40 million pieces instead of 80 million like Nintendo
did with the DS, popular and small are really relative.

For a certain segment of gamers, NetHack is popular, but OTOH NetHack
isn't really competing with other games. That's specific to OSS games.
They usually don't have to be sold and so don't need to appeal to a
large group.


Interestingly, it looks like NetHack might someday lose its place as
the top roguelike game to Dwarf Fortress:
